I came back to my quiet apartment.
I opened my laptop and made a video call to Mexico.
My mother answered the call immediately.
She saw me and she smiled nicely.
"Hello Mom, how are you?"
I asked respectfully.
"I am fine, Maya."
"You look happy today," Mom said.
"Yes Mom."
"I played badminton with friends today," I said.
"Very nice!"
"Last week you were very busy," Mom said.
"Yes, but today I got time," I told her.
"After playing I drank cutting chai with friends," I said smiling.
"Oh wow!"
"Did you all just drink tea or did you chat?"
Mom asked.
"We chatted a lot," I answered.
"My friends asked me about my first days," I said.
"Then what did you tell them?"
Mom asked eagerly.
"I told them the story from January," I answered.
"I told them everything about how I came to Mumbai in January."
